{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit 3495, merged d5f10d1d2c8. Root cause: verify-opcert composed config from the repo root, so the change's own rebar.toml was the project layer for require_environment, opcert_enforce_since, trusted_opcert_keys and tracker.dir; plan review also found the read-time sync.pull lookup in ensure_fresh read the working tree. Fix: _opcert_gate_config.gate_config reads the project layer committed on origin/main, the run binds it as the operation snapshot under local_read_context, and verify-identity.yml fetches main first. Checked on merged main: tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py + test_verify_opcert*.py 23 passed; the attack test exits 0 on the pre-fix gate; check_mechanism_delta --check exits 0; _config_schema.py unchanged. make verify green locally (21573 + 226 passed). Not done here: docs/llm-framework.md:1063 still says the trust list never lives in the repository without mentioning the base-branch rule (plan-review advisory); a show_ticket exception still drops a ticket from scope in verify_opcert.cli (pre-existing)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795244217799371001,"uuid":"14ac51c8-09c8-499d-ae1d-a60215cd46f4"}